u know made their  lives really miserable discredit them  followed their families ran one of their  fathers off the road you know what can  happen now which might have happened is  the kind of dr. nasir moment with USA  Gymnastics where the victims can  confront the victimizer one after  another Julie the US attorney Jeffrey  Berman has made a point of saying the  investigation will continue  where does this case go now well they're  going to look at his accomplices our  so-called alleged accomplices there was  a lot of information as you know that  was released just on Friday yes about  how this operation now is sort of  released in a very strange way because  it wasn't really in sequence but because  I studied all the other documents I  could kind of piece it together a little  bit but it sort of is the framework for  a real sex trafficking operation and now  we know that they're not only just  looking at this at the human trafficking  part of it they're also looking at the  money trail you know and they're looking  at where his money is how he got his  money and hoping that that will lead  them also down another path to finding  who helped him if you were one of his  accomplices at this point would you be  more nervous now that he is dead well  yeah yes I think so because mr. Behrman  is gonna have to start looking at other  people not that he wasn't before but  he's going to probably make a couple of  these other people do the centerpiece of  his case now he killed himself allegedly  after the release of some very damning  documents about him was there anything  in those documents that surprised you I  think some of the names you know we knew  some of those names they had been out  there before because the police  investigation had uncovered a lot of  message pads and you know we also know  he had a epstein had a black book with a  lot of famous people's names on them but  this was really their names in  particular that surprised you well I  think anytime you have someone as  powerful powerful as George Mitchell  for example former senator and Senate  Minority Leader and and Bill Richardson  the governor of New Mexico I think any  time with both of whom by the way all of  these people have denied that they have  not been charged and they have not been  charged and all of them have vigorously  denied that they were involved but you  know when you have a couple of different  depositions and you have that this woman  describing what happened and how it  happened to some degree where it  happened  I'm sure that that's something that  prosecutors are gonna look ok there are  more there are more documents to be  released Julie correct that's correct  you think more people will come forward  it's hard to say it depends on what they  find with the suicide you know at first  I thought that suicide do you believe  that it wasn't suicide there are a lot  of questions about that as well like you  know is he set up to commit suicide or  did he actually take his life a lot of  questions about and the timing of it  what what is your take on it when you  first heard it what was your take well I  thought he probably committed suicide  but then again I you know I covered  Florida prisons for a very long time and  I know the way things work in prisons  and it's very easy to set something up -  I'm not trying to fuel a conspiracy  theory here at all but it is very easy  to set something up to look like a  suicide I'm not saying that happened but  I mean you know I think we have to wait  for the authorities to do their  investigation first well all right Julie  brown thank you very good to have you at  the table
 

